IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `ei6-part-9-coming-into-force`
IMPORT `ei6-schedule-ii-table`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), Schedule II (Section 190), Interim Provisions: paragraphs 1 to 17
-- (paragraph 18, the interim Schedule I, is in ei6-schedule-ii-table). Written by piece ei6 (Sonnet 5.5) on 2026-10-24.
-- Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation current to 2026-09-30; nothing here is
-- claimed to be verified against the official text.
--
-- Seat: a person whose claim or employment falls between June 30, 1996 and January 5, 1997, and who asks what the
-- interim law gave them. Few such questions arise today, but the text is in force and decides them.
--
-- THE GATE. Under s 190(4), Schedule II applies in place of the provisions listed in s 190(2) and (3) from June 30, 1996
-- until each comes into force. Every rule takes the day it is applied to and calls `s 190(4) Schedule II applies in
-- place of the provision on the day` (ei6-part-9-coming-into-force) with the provision it replaces. Paragraph 6 also
-- continues under s 190(5). Outside the gate a rule answers NOTHING (or FALSE for a yes/no question): the section of the
-- Act itself decides (pieces ei1 to ei4), and the interim rule says nothing.
--
-- NAMES. Each rule begins "Schedule II para N s M ..." with the paragraph number and the section it replaces, so that
-- none of them can clash with the rule that another piece writes for section M itself.
--
-- NOT ENCODED (NOTES.md, coverage table, `inert`): paragraph 2 (the power to make regulations excluding employment from
-- insurable employment, in place of subsection 5(6)); paragraph 6, subsection 14(4) (the power to make regulations
-- defining dependants and fixing weekly insurable earnings); paragraph 16 (the power to make regulations in place of
-- paragraph 108(1)(h)).

§ `Paragraph 1 - section 4: the maximum insurable earnings`

-- (1): the maximum yearly insurable earnings is $39,000 for 1996, for the purposes of section 17, subsection 82(2) and
-- sections 95 and 145. (2): the maximum weekly insurable earnings is $750 for the purposes of this Act.
-- src:3250 | 4 (1) For the purposes of section 17, subsection 82(2) and sections 95 and 145, the maximum yearly insurable earnings is $39,000 for 1996.
@ref Employment Insurance Act Schedule II para 1, s 4(1) (src:3250)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Schedule II para 1 s 4(1) the maximum yearly insurable earnings` IS
    IF     `s 190(4) Schedule II applies in place of the provision on the day` "section 4" day
       AND `s 2(1) the year containing` day EQUALS 1996
    THEN JUST 39000
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:3252 | (2) For the purposes of this Act, the maximum weekly insurable earnings is $750.
@ref Employment Insurance Act Schedule II para 1, s 4(2) (src:3252)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Schedule II para 1 s 4(2) the maximum weekly insurable earnings` IS
    IF `s 190(4) Schedule II applies in place of the provision on the day` "section 4" day
    THEN JUST 750
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Paragraph 3 - the definitions of major attachment claimant and minor attachment claimant`

-- src:3264 | major attachment claimant means a claimant who qualifies to receive benefits and has been employed in insurable employment for 20 or more weeks in the claimant’s qualifying period; (prestataire de la première catégorie)
@ref Employment Insurance Act Schedule II para 3 (src:3264)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `qualifies to receive benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of weeks of insurable employment in the claimant's qualifying period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Schedule II para 3 major attachment claimant` IF
        `s 190(4) Schedule II applies in place of the provision on the day` "the definition major attachment claimant in subsection 6(1)" day
    AND `qualifies to receive benefits`
    AND `the number of weeks of insurable employment in the claimant's qualifying period` AT LEAST 20

-- src:3265 | minor attachment claimant means a claimant who qualifies to receive benefits and has been employed in insurable employment for fewer than 20 weeks in the claimant’s qualifying period; (prestataire de la deuxième catégorie)
@ref Employment Insurance Act Schedule II para 3 (src:3265)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `qualifies to receive benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of weeks of insurable employment in the claimant's qualifying period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Schedule II para 3 minor attachment claimant` IF
        `s 190(4) Schedule II applies in place of the provision on the day` "the definition minor attachment claimant in subsection 6(1)" day
    AND `qualifies to receive benefits`
    AND `the number of weeks of insurable employment in the claimant's qualifying period` LESS THAN 20

§ `Paragraph 4 - section 7: when benefits are payable`

-- (1): unemployment benefits are payable to an insured person who qualifies to receive them.
-- src:3268 | 7 (1) Unemployment benefits are payable as provided in this Part to an insured person who qualifies to receive them.
@ref Employment Insurance Act Schedule II para 4, s 7(1) (src:3268)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `is an insured person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `qualifies to receive the benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Schedule II para 4 s 7(1) unemployment benefits are payable to the insured person` IF
        `s 190(4) Schedule II applies in place of the provision on the day` "section 7" day
    AND `is an insured person`
    AND `qualifies to receive the benefits`

-- (2): the table of required weeks, by the regional rate of unemployment. The twelve bands of the keel's `Rate band`
-- are read as the nine rows of this table: bands 9 to 12 are "more than 13%".
-- src:3274 | Regional Rate of Unemployment | Required Number of Weeks of Insurable Employment
-- src:3275 | 6% and under | 20
-- src:3276 | more than 6% but not more than 7% | 19
-- src:3277 | more than 7% but not more than 8% | 18
-- src:3278 | more than 8% but not more than 9% | 17
-- src:3279 | more than 9% but not more than 10% | 16
-- src:3280 | more than 10% but not more than 11% | 15
-- src:3281 | more than 11% but not more than 12% | 14
-- src:3282 | more than 12% but not more than 13% | 13
-- src:3283 | more than 13% | 12
@ref Employment Insurance Act Schedule II para 4, s 7(2) (src:3274-3283)
GIVEN rate IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Schedule II para 4 s 7(2) the required number of weeks of insurable employment` IS
    CONSIDER `the band of the regional rate of unemployment` rate
    WHEN `6% and under`                        THEN 20
    WHEN `more than 6% but not more than 7%`   THEN 19
    WHEN `more than 7% but not more than 8%`   THEN 18
    WHEN `more than 8% but not more than 9%`   THEN 17
    WHEN `more than 9% but not more than 10%`  THEN 16
    WHEN `more than 10% but not more than 11%` THEN 15
    WHEN `more than 11% but not more than 12%` THEN 14
    WHEN `more than 12% but not more than 13%` THEN 13
    OTHERWISE                                       12

-- (2) and (3): an insured person, other than a new entrant or re-entrant, qualifies if they have had an interruption of
-- earnings from employment and at least the required weeks in the qualifying period; a new entrant or re-entrant, if they
-- have had an interruption of earnings from employment and 26 or more weeks.
-- src:3270 | (2) An insured person, other than a new entrant or a re-entrant to the labour force, qualifies if the person
-- src:3271 | (a) has had an interruption of earnings from employment; and
-- src:3272 | (b) has had during their qualifying period at least the number of weeks of insurable employment set out in the following table in relation to the regional rate of unemployment that applies to the person.
-- src:3285 | (3) An insured person who is a new entrant or a re-entrant to the labour force qualifies if the person
-- src:3286 | (a) has had an interruption of earnings from employment; and
-- src:3287 | (b) has had 26 or more weeks of insurable employment during their qualifying period.
@ref Employment Insurance Act Schedule II para 4, s 7(2), (3) (src:3270-3272) (src:3285-3287)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `is a new entrant or a re-entrant to the labour force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `has had an interruption of earnings from employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of weeks of insurable employment in the qualifying period` IS A NUMBER
      `the regional rate of unemployment that applies to the person` IS A NUMBER  -- out of range: reg 17 (piece er1)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Schedule II para 4 s 7(2) and (3) the insured person qualifies to receive benefits` IF
        `s 190(4) Schedule II applies in place of the provision on the day` "section 7" day
    AND `has had an interruption of earnings from employment`
    AND (   (    `is a new entrant or a re-entrant to the labour force`
             AND `the number of weeks of insurable employment in the qualifying period` AT LEAST 26)
         OR (    NOT (`is a new entrant or a re-entrant to the labour force`)
             AND `the number of weeks of insurable employment in the qualifying period` AT LEAST `Schedule II para 4 s 7(2) the required number of weeks of insurable employment` `the regional rate of unemployment that applies to the person`))

-- (4) and (5): a new entrant or re-entrant has, in the last 52 weeks before the qualifying period, fewer than 14 weeks of
-- insurable employment, of benefits paid or payable, of prescribed weeks relating to employment in the labour force, or
-- of any combination of them; and a week counted under one of (a), (b) and (c) is not counted under another. The
-- reading taken is the combination (paragraph (d)): the three counts, with no week counted twice, together are fewer
-- than 14 (fork F-ei6-15 in NOTES.md).
-- src:3289 | (4) An insured person is a new entrant or a re-entrant to the labour force if, during the last 52 weeks before their qualifying period, the person has had fewer than 14
-- src:3290 | (a) weeks of insurable employment;
-- src:3291 | (b) weeks for which benefits have been paid or were payable to the person;
-- src:3292 | (c) prescribed weeks that relate to employment in the labour force; or
-- src:3293 | (d) weeks comprised of any combination of those weeks.
-- src:3294 | Computation of weeks
-- src:3295 | (5) For the purposes of subsection (4), a week that is taken into account under any of paragraphs (4)(a), (b) or (c) may not be taken into account under the other.
@ref Employment Insurance Act Schedule II para 4, s 7(4), (5) (src:3289-3295)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `the number of weeks of insurable employment in the last 52 weeks before the qualifying period` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of weeks for which benefits have been paid or were payable in those 52 weeks, not already counted` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of prescribed weeks that relate to employment in the labour force in those 52 weeks, not already counted` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Schedule II para 4 s 7(4) the insured person is a new entrant or a re-entrant to the labour force` IF
        `s 190(4) Schedule II applies in place of the provision on the day` "section 7" day
    AND (  `the number of weeks of insurable employment in the last 52 weeks before the qualifying period`
         PLUS `the number of weeks for which benefits have been paid or were payable in those 52 weeks, not already counted`
         PLUS `the number of prescribed weeks that relate to employment in the labour force in those 52 weeks, not already counted`) LESS THAN 14

-- (6): a claimant is not qualified if it is jointly determined that the claimant must first exhaust or terminate benefit
-- rights under the laws of another jurisdiction, as provided by Article VI of the Agreement Between Canada and the
-- United States Respecting Unemployment Insurance, signed on March 6 and 12, 1942.
-- src:3297 | (6) A claimant is not qualified to receive benefits if it is jointly determined that the claimant must first exhaust or terminate benefit rights under the laws of another jurisdiction, as provided by Article VI of the Agreement Between Canada and the United States Respecting Unemployment Insurance, signed on March 6 and 12, 1942.
@ref Employment Insurance Act Schedule II para 4, s 7(6) (src:3297)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `it is jointly determined that the claimant must first exhaust or terminate benefit rights under the laws of another jurisdiction as provided by Article VI of the Agreement Between Canada and the United States Respecting Unemployment Insurance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Schedule II para 4 s 7(6) the claimant is not qualified to receive benefits` IF
        `s 190(4) Schedule II applies in place of the provision on the day` "section 7" day
    AND `it is jointly determined that the claimant must first exhaust or terminate benefit rights under the laws of another jurisdiction as provided by Article VI of the Agreement Between Canada and the United States Respecting Unemployment Insurance`

§ `Paragraph 5 - subsection 12(2): the general maximum`

-- The maximum number of weeks is determined by the table in Schedule I (here the interim Schedule I of paragraph 18) by
-- the regional rate of unemployment and the number of weeks of insurable employment in the qualifying period.
-- src:3300 | (2) The maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid in a benefit period because of any reasons other than those referred to in subsection (3) shall be determined in accordance with the table in Schedule I by reference to the regional rate of unemployment that applies to the claimant and the number of weeks of insurable employment of the claimant in their qualifying period.
@ref Employment Insurance Act Schedule II para 5, s 12(2) (src:3300)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `the number of weeks of insurable employment in the qualifying period` IS A NUMBER
      `the regional rate of unemployment that applies to the claimant` IS A NUMBER  -- out of range: reg 17 (piece er1)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Schedule II para 5 s 12(2) the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid in a benefit period` IS
    IF `s 190(4) Schedule II applies in place of the provision on the day` "subsection 12(2)" day
    THEN `Schedule II para 18 the maximum number of weeks of benefit` `the number of weeks of insurable employment in the qualifying period` `the regional rate of unemployment that applies to the claimant`
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Paragraph 6 - section 14: the rate of weekly benefits`

-- Paragraph 6 applies from June 30, 1996 until section 14 comes into force (s 190(4)), and continues, for a claimant whose
-- benefit period began on or after June 30, 1996 and before January 5, 1997, in place of sections 14, 16 and 17 (s 190(5)).
-- src:3195 | (4) The provisions set out in Schedule II apply in place of the provisions listed in subsections (2) and (3) from June 30, 1996 until the coming into force of those provisions.
-- src:3196 | Continuing application of benefit rate provision
-- src:3197 | (5) The provisions enacted by section 6 of Schedule II continue to apply in place of sections 14, 16 and 17 of this Act to claimants whose benefit periods begin on or after June 30, 1996 and before January 5, 1997.
@ref Employment Insurance Act Schedule II para 6 and s 190(4), (5) (src:3195-3197)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `the first day of the benefit period` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Schedule II para 6 applies in place of sections 14, 16 and 17` IF
       `s 190(4) Schedule II applies in place of the provision on the day` "section 14" day
    OR `s 190(5) paragraph 6 of Schedule II continues to apply in place of sections 14, 16 and 17` `the first day of the benefit period`

-- (1): the rate is 55% of the average weekly insurable earnings (a); or, where the prescribed circumstances for
-- dependants exist or the Commission is of the opinion that the claimant or spouse supports dependants (b), (i) 60% if
-- those earnings do not exceed 50% of the maximum weekly insurable earnings, (ii) the greater of 55% and $225 if they
-- exceed that half; to a maximum of $413. Percentages of earnings are rounded to the nearest dollar by s 6(2) (fork
-- F-ei6-16 in NOTES.md). The maximum weekly insurable earnings is $750 (paragraph 1), so the half is $375.
-- src:3303 | 14 (1) The rate of weekly benefits payable to a claimant is an amount calculated as follows, to a maximum of $413:
-- src:3304 | (a) 55% of the claimant’s average weekly insurable earnings, in the case of a claimant in respect of whom paragraph (b) does not apply; or
-- src:3305 | (b) in any case where it is established, in such manner as the Commission may direct, that the prescribed circumstances exist in relation to one or more persons who are dependants of the claimant or their spouse or that, in the opinion of the Commission, even though the prescribed circumstances do not exist, the claimant or their spouse supports one or more persons who are dependants of the claimant or of their spouse,
-- src:3306 | (i) 60% of the claimant’s average weekly insurable earnings, if those earnings do not exceed 50% of the maximum weekly insurable earnings for the year in which the benefit period is established, or
-- src:3307 | (ii) the greater of 55% of the claimant’s average weekly insurable earnings and $225, if the claimant’s average weekly insurable earnings exceed 50% of the maximum weekly insurable earnings for that year.
@ref Employment Insurance Act Schedule II para 6, s 14(1) (src:3303-3307)
GIVEN `Schedule II paragraph 6 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant's average weekly insurable earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `it is established that the prescribed circumstances exist in relation to one or more persons who are dependants of the claimant or their spouse, or, in the opinion of the Commission, the claimant or their spouse supports one or more such persons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Schedule II para 6 s 14(1) the rate of weekly benefits` IS
    IF `Schedule II paragraph 6 applies`
    THEN JUST (IF `the calculated rate` GREATER THAN 413 THEN 413 ELSE `the calculated rate`)
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `the calculated rate` MEANS
            IF NOT (`it is established that the prescribed circumstances exist in relation to one or more persons who are dependants of the claimant or their spouse, or, in the opinion of the Commission, the claimant or their spouse supports one or more such persons`)
            THEN `s 6(2) and s 152.01(5) amount rounded to the nearest dollar` (55% TIMES `the claimant's average weekly insurable earnings`)
            ELSE IF `the claimant's average weekly insurable earnings` AT MOST 375
                 THEN `s 6(2) and s 152.01(5) amount rounded to the nearest dollar` (60% TIMES `the claimant's average weekly insurable earnings`)
                 ELSE (IF `s 6(2) and s 152.01(5) amount rounded to the nearest dollar` (55% TIMES `the claimant's average weekly insurable earnings`) GREATER THAN 225
                       THEN `s 6(2) and s 152.01(5) amount rounded to the nearest dollar` (55% TIMES `the claimant's average weekly insurable earnings`)
                       ELSE 225)

-- (2): the average weekly insurable earnings of a major attachment claimant are the insurable earnings in the last 20
-- weeks of insurable employment in their qualifying period divided by 20.
-- src:3309 | (2) The average weekly insurable earnings of a major attachment claimant are the insurable earnings in the last 20 weeks of insurable employment in their qualifying period divided by 20.
@ref Employment Insurance Act Schedule II para 6, s 14(2) (src:3309)
GIVEN `Schedule II paragraph 6 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the insurable earnings in the last 20 weeks of insurable employment in the claimant's qualifying period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Schedule II para 6 s 14(2) the average weekly insurable earnings of a major attachment claimant` IS
    IF `Schedule II paragraph 6 applies`
    THEN JUST (`the insurable earnings in the last 20 weeks of insurable employment in the claimant's qualifying period` DIVIDED BY 20)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (3): for a minor attachment claimant, the insurable earnings in the qualifying period divided by the larger of (a)
-- the number of weeks of insurable employment in that period and (b) the divisor of the table for the regional rate.
-- src:3314 | TABLE
-- src:3315 | Regional Rate of Unemployment | Divisor
-- src:3316 | not more than 8% | 20
-- src:3317 | more than 8% but not more than 9% | 19
-- src:3318 | more than 9% but not more than 10% | 18
-- src:3319 | more than 10% but not more than 11% | 17
-- src:3320 | more than 11% but not more than 12% | 16
-- src:3321 | more than 12% but not more than 13% | 15
-- src:3322 | more than 13% | 14
@ref Employment Insurance Act Schedule II para 6, s 14(3) (src:3314-3322)
GIVEN rate IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Schedule II para 6 s 14(3) the divisor for the regional rate of unemployment` IS
    CONSIDER `the band of the regional rate of unemployment` rate
    WHEN `6% and under`                        THEN 20
    WHEN `more than 6% but not more than 7%`   THEN 20
    WHEN `more than 7% but not more than 8%`   THEN 20
    WHEN `more than 8% but not more than 9%`   THEN 19
    WHEN `more than 9% but not more than 10%`  THEN 18
    WHEN `more than 10% but not more than 11%` THEN 17
    WHEN `more than 11% but not more than 12%` THEN 16
    WHEN `more than 12% but not more than 13%` THEN 15
    OTHERWISE                                       14

-- src:3311 | (3) The average weekly insurable earnings of a minor attachment claimant are the insurable earnings in their qualifying period divided by the larger of the following divisors:
-- src:3312 | (a) the divisor that equals the number of weeks of insurable employment in their qualifying period, and
-- src:3313 | (b) the divisor determined in accordance with the following table by reference to the applicable regional rate of unemployment.
@ref Employment Insurance Act Schedule II para 6, s 14(3) (src:3311-3313)
GIVEN `Schedule II paragraph 6 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the insurable earnings in the claimant's qualifying period` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of weeks of insurable employment in the claimant's qualifying period` IS A NUMBER
      `the regional rate of unemployment that applies to the claimant` IS A NUMBER  -- out of range: reg 17 (piece er1)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Schedule II para 6 s 14(3) the average weekly insurable earnings of a minor attachment claimant` IS
    IF `Schedule II paragraph 6 applies`
    THEN JUST (`the insurable earnings in the claimant's qualifying period` DIVIDED BY `the larger divisor`)
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `the larger divisor` MEANS
            IF `the number of weeks of insurable employment in the claimant's qualifying period` GREATER THAN `Schedule II para 6 s 14(3) the divisor for the regional rate of unemployment` `the regional rate of unemployment that applies to the claimant`
            THEN `the number of weeks of insurable employment in the claimant's qualifying period`
            ELSE `Schedule II para 6 s 14(3) the divisor for the regional rate of unemployment` `the regional rate of unemployment that applies to the claimant`

§ `Paragraphs 7 to 11 - sections 19(2), 28(4), 30, 31 and 32`

-- 7: in place of subsection 19(2): there is deducted from the benefits for a week of unemployment the amount, if any, of
-- the earnings that exceeds 25% of the weekly rate of benefit. NOTHING means there is no excess to deduct.
-- src:3332 | (2) Subject to subsections (3) and (4), if a claimant has earnings during any other week of unemployment, there shall be deducted from the benefits payable to the claimant in that week the amount, if any, of the earnings that exceeds 25% of their weekly rate of benefit.
@ref Employment Insurance Act Schedule II para 7, s 19(2) (src:3332)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `the claimant's earnings during the week` IS A NUMBER
      `the claimant's weekly rate of benefit` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Schedule II para 7 s 19(2) the amount deducted from the benefits payable for the week` IS
    IF     `s 190(4) Schedule II applies in place of the provision on the day` "subsection 19(2)" day
       AND `the claimant's earnings during the week` GREATER THAN 25% TIMES `the claimant's weekly rate of benefit`
    THEN JUST (`the claimant's earnings during the week` MINUS 25% TIMES `the claimant's weekly rate of benefit`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- 8: in place of subsection 28(4): no weeks of disqualification are carried forward against a claimant who has had 20 or
-- more weeks of insurable employment since the event giving rise to the disqualification.
-- src:3335 | (4) No weeks of disqualification shall be carried forward against a claimant who has had 20 or more weeks of insurable employment since the event giving rise to the disqualification.
@ref Employment Insurance Act Schedule II para 8, s 28(4) (src:3335)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `the number of weeks of insurable employment since the event giving rise to the disqualification` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Schedule II para 8 s 28(4) no weeks of disqualification are carried forward against the claimant` IF
        `s 190(4) Schedule II applies in place of the provision on the day` "subsection 28(4)" day
    AND `the number of weeks of insurable employment since the event giving rise to the disqualification` AT LEAST 20

-- 9(1): in place of paragraph 30(1)(a): the claimant has, since losing or leaving the employment, been employed in
-- insurable employment for the number of weeks required by section 7 to qualify for benefits.
-- src:3337 | (a) the claimant has, since losing or leaving the employment, been employed in insurable employment for the number of weeks required by section 7 to qualify for benefits; or
@ref Employment Insurance Act Schedule II para 9(1), s 30(1)(a) (src:3337)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `the number of weeks of insurable employment since losing or leaving the employment` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of weeks required by section 7 to qualify for benefits` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Schedule II para 9(1) s 30(1)(a) the claimant has been employed in insurable employment for the number of weeks required by section 7` IF
        `s 190(4) Schedule II applies in place of the provision on the day` "paragraph 30(1)(a)" day
    AND `the number of weeks of insurable employment since losing or leaving the employment` AT LEAST `the number of weeks required by section 7 to qualify for benefits`

-- 9(2): in place of subsections 30(5) and (6). (5): on an initial claim after losing or leaving an employment as
-- described in (1), weeks of insurable employment from that or any other employment before the day the employment was
-- lost or left, and weeks in any employment the claimant later loses or leaves as described in (1), may not be used for
-- subsection 7(2) or (3). (6): no weeks in an employment lost or left as described in (1) may be used for subsection
-- 12(2) or section 14.
-- src:3340 | (5) Where a claimant who has lost or left an employment as described in subsection (1) makes an initial claim for benefits, the following weeks of insurable employment may not be used for the purposes of subsection 7(2) or (3):
-- src:3341 | (a) weeks of insurable employment from that or any other employment before the day on which that employment was lost or left; and
-- src:3342 | (b) weeks of insurable employment in any employment that the claimant subsequently loses or leaves, as described in subsection (1).
@ref Employment Insurance Act Schedule II para 9(2), s 30(5) (src:3340-3342)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `the weeks are weeks of insurable employment from that or any other employment before the day on which that employment was lost or left` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the weeks are weeks of insurable employment in any employment that the claimant subsequently loses or leaves, as described in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Schedule II para 9(2) s 30(5) the weeks may not be used for the purposes of subsection 7(2) or (3)` IF
        `s 190(4) Schedule II applies in place of the provision on the day` "subsection 30(5)" day
    AND (   `the weeks are weeks of insurable employment from that or any other employment before the day on which that employment was lost or left`
         OR `the weeks are weeks of insurable employment in any employment that the claimant subsequently loses or leaves, as described in subsection (1)`)

-- src:3344 | (6) No weeks of insurable employment in any employment that a claimant loses or leaves as described in subsection (1) may be used for the purposes of subsection 12(2) or section 14.
@ref Employment Insurance Act Schedule II para 9(2), s 30(6) (src:3344)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `the weeks are weeks of insurable employment in an employment that the claimant loses or leaves as described in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Schedule II para 9(2) s 30(6) the weeks may not be used for the purposes of subsection 12(2) or section 14` IF
        `s 190(4) Schedule II applies in place of the provision on the day` "subsection 30(6)" day
    AND `the weeks are weeks of insurable employment in an employment that the claimant loses or leaves as described in subsection (1)`

-- 10 and 11: in place of paragraphs 31(c) and 32(2)(c): the claimant, after the beginning of the period of suspension
-- (or leave), accumulates with another employer the number of weeks of insurable employment required under section 7.
-- src:3346 | (c) the claimant, after the beginning of the period of suspension, accumulates with another employer the number of weeks of insurable employment required under section 7 in order to qualify to receive benefits under this Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Act Schedule II para 10, s 31(c) (src:3346)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `the number of weeks of insurable employment accumulated with another employer after the beginning of the period of suspension` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of weeks required under section 7 to qualify to receive benefits` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Schedule II para 10 s 31(c) the claimant has accumulated with another employer the weeks required under section 7` IF
        `s 190(4) Schedule II applies in place of the provision on the day` "paragraph 31(c)" day
    AND `the number of weeks of insurable employment accumulated with another employer after the beginning of the period of suspension` AT LEAST `the number of weeks required under section 7 to qualify to receive benefits`

-- src:3348 | (c) the claimant, after the beginning of the period of leave, accumulates with another employer the number of weeks of insurable employment required under section 7 in order to qualify to receive benefits under this Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Act Schedule II para 11, s 32(2)(c) (src:3348)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `the number of weeks of insurable employment accumulated with another employer after the beginning of the period of leave` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of weeks required under section 7 to qualify to receive benefits` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Schedule II para 11 s 32(2)(c) the claimant has accumulated with another employer the weeks required under section 7` IF
        `s 190(4) Schedule II applies in place of the provision on the day` "paragraph 32(2)(c)" day
    AND `the number of weeks of insurable employment accumulated with another employer after the beginning of the period of leave` AT LEAST `the number of weeks required under section 7 to qualify to receive benefits`

§ `Paragraphs 12 to 15 - premiums: sections 66, 67, 82(1) and 95`

-- 12: in place of section 66: the premium rate for 1996 is the rate established for that year under section 48.1 of the
-- Unemployment Insurance Act immediately before its repeal (an input: the rate is not in the text).
-- src:3351 | 66 The premium rate for 1996 is the rate established for that year under section 48.1 of the Unemployment Insurance Act immediately before its repeal.
@ref Employment Insurance Act Schedule II para 12, s 66 (src:3351)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `the rate established for 1996 under section 48.1 of the Unemployment Insurance Act immediately before its repeal` IS A NUMBER  -- out of range: nothing; the rate is the former Act's, not in the text
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Schedule II para 12 s 66 the premium rate for 1996` IS
    IF `s 190(4) Schedule II applies in place of the provision on the day` "section 66" day
    THEN JUST `the rate established for 1996 under section 48.1 of the Unemployment Insurance Act immediately before its repeal`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- 13(1), (2): in place of section 67: for every week during which a person is employed in insurable employment, the person
-- pays by deduction, and the employer pays, an amount equal to the percentage of their insurable earnings that the
-- Commission fixes for the year in which the week occurs. The percentages are fixed by the Commission (inputs).
-- src:3354 | 67 (1) For every week during which a person is employed in insurable employment, the person shall pay, by deduction as provided in Part IV, an amount equal to such percentage of their insurable earnings as is fixed by the Commission as the employee’s premium for the year in which that week occurs.
@ref Employment Insurance Act Schedule II para 13, s 67(1) (src:3354)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `is employed in insurable employment during the week` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person's insurable earnings for the week` IS A NUMBER
      `the percentage fixed by the Commission as the employee's premium for the year in which the week occurs` IS A NUMBER  -- out of range: the Commission's decision, not in the text; a fraction
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Schedule II para 13 s 67(1) the employee's premium for the week` IS
    IF     `s 190(4) Schedule II applies in place of the provision on the day` "section 67" day
       AND `is employed in insurable employment during the week`
    THEN JUST (`the person's insurable earnings for the week` TIMES `the percentage fixed by the Commission as the employee's premium for the year in which the week occurs`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:3356 | (2) For every week during which an employer employs a person in insurable employment, the employer shall pay, in respect of that person and in the manner provided in Part IV, an amount equal to such percentage of that person’s insurable earnings as is fixed by the Commission as the employer’s premium payable by employers or a class of employers of which the employer is a member, as the case may be, for the year in which that week occurs.
@ref Employment Insurance Act Schedule II para 13, s 67(2) (src:3356)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `employs a person in insurable employment during the week` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that person's insurable earnings for the week` IS A NUMBER
      `the percentage fixed by the Commission as the employer's premium for the year in which the week occurs` IS A NUMBER  -- out of range: the Commission's decision, not in the text; a fraction
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Schedule II para 13 s 67(2) the employer's premium for the week` IS
    IF     `s 190(4) Schedule II applies in place of the provision on the day` "section 67" day
       AND `employs a person in insurable employment during the week`
    THEN JUST (`that person's insurable earnings for the week` TIMES `the percentage fixed by the Commission as the employer's premium for the year in which the week occurs`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- 13(3): insurable earnings paid in a year after the year in which the insurable employment occurred are, for the
-- insurable earnings and premiums, deemed to have occurred in the year they are paid.
-- src:3358 | (3) Notwithstanding subsections (1) and (2), where insurable earnings are paid to a person in a year after the year in which their insurable employment occurred, all that insurable employment is, for the purposes of calculating insurable earnings and premiums payable in respect of them, deemed to have occurred in the year in which the insurable earnings are paid.
@ref Employment Insurance Act Schedule II para 13, s 67(3) (src:3358)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `the year in which the insurable employment occurred` IS A NUMBER
      `the year in which the insurable earnings are paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Schedule II para 13 s 67(3) the year in which the insurable employment is deemed to have occurred` IS
    IF `s 190(4) Schedule II applies in place of the provision on the day` "section 67" day
    THEN JUST (IF `the year in which the insurable earnings are paid` GREATER THAN `the year in which the insurable employment occurred`
               THEN `the year in which the insurable earnings are paid`
               ELSE `the year in which the insurable employment occurred`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- 14: in place of subsection 82(1): every employer paying remuneration to a person employed in insurable employment shall
-- (a) deduct the prescribed amount as the employee's premium, and (b) remit it with the employer's premium to the
-- Receiver General at the prescribed time and in the prescribed manner. The employee's claim is that the deduction is
-- no more than the prescribed amount; the employer's duty is the deduction and the remittance.
-- src:3361 | 82 (1) Every employer paying remuneration to a person employed by the employer in insurable employment shall
-- src:3362 | (a) deduct the prescribed amount from that remuneration as or on account of the employee’s premium payable by that insured person under section 67 for any weeks in respect of which that remuneration is paid; and
-- src:3363 | (b) remit that amount, together with the employer’s premium payable by the employer under that section for those weeks, to the Receiver General at the prescribed time and in the prescribed manner.
@ref Employment Insurance Act Schedule II para 14, s 82(1) (src:3361-3363)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `the employer pays remuneration to a person employed by the employer in insurable employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Schedule II para 14 s 82(1) the employer must deduct the prescribed amount from the remuneration and remit it` IF
        `s 190(4) Schedule II applies in place of the provision on the day` "subsection 82(1)" day
    AND `the employer pays remuneration to a person employed by the employer in insurable employment`

-- src:3363 | (b) remit that amount, together with the employer’s premium payable by the employer under that section for those weeks, to the Receiver General at the prescribed time and in the prescribed manner.
@ref Employment Insurance Act Schedule II para 14, s 82(1)(b) (src:3363)
GIVEN `the amount deducted as the employee's premium` IS A NUMBER
      `the employer's premium payable by the employer for those weeks` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Schedule II para 14 s 82(1)(b) the amount to be remitted to the Receiver General` IS
    `the amount deducted as the employee's premium` PLUS `the employer's premium payable by the employer for those weeks`

-- 15: in place of section 95. (1): the excess of the amounts deducted for a year over the percentage fixed by the
-- Commission of the person's maximum yearly insurable earnings is an overpayment made by the person. (2): not when the
-- excess occurs only because the remuneration paid in the year is in respect of more than 52 calendar weeks.
-- src:3366 | 95 (1) Where the aggregate of all amounts deducted as required from the insurable earnings of an insured person for a year, whether by one or more employers, on account of that person’s employee’s premiums for that year under this Act exceeds an amount equal to such percentage of the person’s maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year as is fixed by the Commission, the excess is an overpayment made by the person.
-- src:3367 | Limitation — remuneration for more than 52 weeks
-- src:3368 | (2) Notwithstanding subsection (1) and section 3, an overpayment is not created when amounts are deducted and remitted as required from the insurable earnings of an insured person in excess of the percentage of the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year, if the excess occurs by reason only that the remuneration paid to the person in that year is in respect of more than 52 calendar weeks.
@ref Employment Insurance Act Schedule II para 15, s 95(1), (2) (src:3366-3368)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `the aggregate of all amounts deducted from the person's insurable earnings for the year, on account of the employee's premiums` IS A NUMBER
      `the percentage of the person's maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year fixed by the Commission` IS A NUMBER  -- out of range: the Commission's decision, not in the text; a fraction
      `the person's maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the excess occurs only because the remuneration paid to the person in the year is in respect of more than 52 calendar weeks` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Schedule II para 15 s 95 the overpayment made by the person` IS
    IF     `s 190(4) Schedule II applies in place of the provision on the day` "section 95" day
       AND `the aggregate of all amounts deducted from the person's insurable earnings for the year, on account of the employee's premiums` GREATER THAN `the percentage of the person's maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year fixed by the Commission` TIMES `the person's maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year`
       AND NOT (`the excess occurs only because the remuneration paid to the person in the year is in respect of more than 52 calendar weeks`)
    THEN JUST (`the aggregate of all amounts deducted from the person's insurable earnings for the year, on account of the employee's premiums` MINUS `the percentage of the person's maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year fixed by the Commission` TIMES `the person's maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Paragraph 17 - subsection 153.1(3): special benefits under a scheme by regulation`

-- 17: in place of subsection 153.1(3): the scheme established by the regulations may not provide special benefits to
-- persons who (a) have less than 20 weeks of insurable employment in their qualifying period, or (b) are subject to an
-- increase under section 7.1 in the number of hours of insurable employment required to qualify for benefits.
-- src:3377 | (3) The scheme established by the regulations may not provide special benefits to persons who
-- src:3378 | (a) have less than 20 weeks of insurable employment in their qualifying period; or
-- src:3379 | (b) are subject to an increase under section 7.1 in the number of hours of insurable employment required to qualify for benefits.
@ref Employment Insurance Act Schedule II para 17, s 153.1(3) (src:3377-3379)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `the number of weeks of insurable employment in the person's qualifying period` IS A NUMBER
      `is subject to an increase under section 7.1 in the number of hours of insurable employment required to qualify for benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Schedule II para 17 s 153.1(3) the scheme established by the regulations may not provide special benefits to the person` IF
        `s 190(4) Schedule II applies in place of the provision on the day` "subsection 153.1(3)" day
    AND (   `the number of weeks of insurable employment in the person's qualifying period` LESS THAN 20
         OR `is subject to an increase under section 7.1 in the number of hours of insurable employment required to qualify for benefits`)
